        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Keguang Xu",
          "email": "kxu@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-11-23 06:21:40.000000000",
          "tz": 480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21160 lod: reuse earlier parity OSTs across raid sets",
        "message": "LU-21160 lod: reuse earlier parity OSTs across raid sets\n\nMulti-raidset parity reused data OSTs from other sets, so\nlod_stripe_count_min() returned 0 unique OSTs.  Each set can\nreuse at most (c - k) such OSTs; when p is larger, the rest\nmust be unique.  With sibling -c mirrors filling the pool at\nspeed 0, resync then hit ENOSPC before raising speed.\n\nThe unique OSTs fill raid set 0 first, and lod_ec_add_parities()\ncould only reuse data OSTs, so later sets still ran short even\nwhen enough unique OSTs were free, e.g. -c 4 --ec 1+4 on 8 OSTs,\nor --ec 2+3 next to a sibling mirror that leaves 2 OSTs free.\n\nLet lod_ec_add_parities() fall back to the unique parity OSTs of\nearlier raid sets after the data OSTs, with the checks shared in\nlod_ec_parity_reuse_ok().  Unique OSTs then need not be disjoint\nbetween sets, so require only the largest per-set deficit\nmax(0, p - (c - esc_k0)) before reuse.  sanity-ec 8q covers the\nminimum next to a sibling mirror, 8r the reuse of earlier parity\nOSTs.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-ec ostcount=8\nFixes: c53abca9f9ee (\"LU-19852 lod: raidset aware stripe allocator\")\nSigned-off-by: Keguang Xu <kxu@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: Cursor:Composer\nAssisted-by: Augment:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Ifca03e16c692665e618722825b0f9926febb39f9\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
